# --- third-party code, rebuilt by tools/bootstrap.sh ------------------------
# extern/ must stay strictly pristine: we do not version it, we re-clone it at
# the pinned commits. Two exceptions, which have no repository to clone from and
# are required to build:
extern/*
!extern/tsf/
!extern/soundfont/

# --- bulky corpora and tools, specific to the machine -----------------------
# Chiptunes/  : ~750 MB, the personal test corpus
# Dolphin-x64/: ~420 MB, portable Dolphin (version tested: 2606)
#
# The leading / is NOT decorative: without it a gitignore pattern applies at
# every level, and on Windows case is ignored -- so "Chiptunes/" made
# test/chiptunes/, the test set, disappear.
/Chiptunes/
/KEYGENMUSiC MusicPack/
# The culled pack, the one that goes onto the card -- 738 MB, plus its archive.
# Without these two lines, an absent-minded "git add -A" takes the whole corpus
# with it.
/KEYGENMUSiC MusicPack GC Edition/
/KEYGENMUSiC MusicPack GC Edition.7z
# What the cull set aside (docs/pack-dropped.txt). Moved, not deleted -- but it
# has no business in the repository either.
/Pack-rebut/
/Dolphin-x64/

# --- build products ---------------------------------------------------------
build-gc/
build-host/

# Leftovers from a libxmp build launched from the root: the objects landed here
# instead of build-host/libxmp/. Harmless, but useless.
/*.o

*.exe
*.a
*.elf
*.dol
*.map
# ... except the test set's .dol, which must be ready to use:
!test/gc-chiptune.dol

# --- the study journal, deliberately not published --------------------------
# docs/STATUS.md is the chronological account of the whole investigation: every
# fault found, every measurement, every decision reversed. It is written for
# whoever maintains this, not for whoever uses it, and it stays on the machine.
#
# The source comments and the other documents cite its sections by number
# (§13, §12.20, §20...). Those citations are left as they are: they are worth
# something to the maintainer, who has the file, and they cost a reader nothing
# -- README says where they point. What must NOT happen is a markdown LINK to
# it, which would 404 in the published tree.
#
# ⚠️ Ignoring it here does not remove it from a history that already contains
# it. The 1.0.0 tree was published as a single fresh commit for exactly that
# reason; the previous history is on the local branch pre-1.0.0-history.
docs/STATUS.md

# --- misc -------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
